+## Patch 8: architecture-private text model wrapper
+
+Patch 8 composes the verified one-token decoder layer into a complete
+architecture-private text model. It does not remove the public loader guard and
+does not publish a WASTE manifest.
+
+The wrapper follows the official text path exactly:
+
+1. fetch one embedding row;
+2. apply `embed_norm` RMSNorm;
+3. execute every configured decoder layer;
+4. apply the final RMSNorm;
+5. divide hidden states by `logits_mup_width_multiplier`;
+6. multiply by the independent unembedding table;
+7. return only `unpadded_vocab_size` logits.
+
+Both vocabulary tables can be resident or supplied one row at a time by a
+callback. This preserves bounded RAM and reflects the official implementation's
+explicit statement that embed and unembed are separate checkpoint tensors.
+Routed experts continue to use the decoder layer's expert callback, so the
+model wrapper does not weaken WASTE's streamed-expert design.
+
+All recurrent storage is caller-owned. Local layers allocate K/V rings no
+larger than `min(context_capacity, sliding_window)`; global layers allocate the
+requested bounded context. Four depthwise convolution states are allocated per
+layer. Storage arithmetic is overflow checked and invalid capacities return
+zero or fail before mutation.
+
+Synthetic end-to-end differential tests cover resident and callback-backed
+embedding/unembedding tables, complete two-layer logits, reset behavior,
+sequential positions, context bounds, and output-buffer bounds. These tests do
+not constitute official Inkling-Small parity; official Small checkpoint assets
+remain unavailable.
